$DIR/test.p:36:12: cannot range over s (variable of struct type S): S has no method All returning an iterator
    A for range loop over a value that is not a string, integer, array, slice,
    map, channel or function calls the value's All method and ranges over the
    iterator it returns, an iter.Seq or iter.Seq2. This type has no All method.
    Give the type an All method that returns an iterator, or range over one of
    its other iterators.
    Library containers such as vec.Vec and hash.Map are structs, not built-in
    types, so the loop asks them for an iterator by name. vec.Vec and hash.Map
    have All, so they range like Go's slices and maps.
    Add an All method:
        func (t *T) All() iter.Seq2[string, int] {
            return func(yield func(string, int) bool) {
                // call yield for each key and value
            }
        }
    (see "For statements" in the Plutonium spec, section 12.10)
    (run "pluto explain E2456" for a longer explanation)
